{"arena": "A", "t": 1792869703.7, "seq": 33, "op": "mutate", "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "cost": 0.00103725, "parents": ["A16"], "log": {"edges": [["bag_ready", "altar_eta", "call"]], "n_edges": 1, "editable": ["r11", "s11"], "llm": {"in": 4595, "out": 1052, "cache_read": 5175, "cache_write": 0, "seconds": 5.2, "stop": "end_turn"}, "reply": "This mutation makes `altar_eta` prefer altars outside monolith reach, since those are the ones the bank walk targets. It falls back to the original calculation when no safe altar tile exists. `bag_ready` is unchanged.\n\n```python\n@gene(\"s11\", \"turns to stand next to a safe altar we can tribute at; else any unlocked altar (1000 if none)\", parents=[\"s11\"])\ndef altar_eta() -> Num:\n    ring = safe_altar_ring()\n    if size(ring) > 0:\n        return eta(dist(here(), nearest(ring, here())), me().move_speed)\n    d = min((max(0, dist(here(), a) - 1) for a in altars() - locked_altars()), default=-1)\n    if d < 0:\n        return 1000\n    return eta(d, me().move_speed)\n```"}, "error": "GenomeError: altar_eta line 482: cannot assign to ring", "birth": 18, "accepted": false, "fingerprint": null}
