{"arena": "A", "t": 1792869720.4, "seq": 37, "op": "mutate", "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "cost": 0.0014948499999999998, "parents": ["A9"], "log": {"edges": [["r_pass", "foe_in_reach", "call"], ["shard_left", "shard_until", "call"]], "n_edges": 2, "editable": ["a15", "a16", "r6", "s5"], "llm": {"in": 4746, "out": 1937, "cache_read": 5175, "cache_write": 0, "seconds": 9.1, "stop": "end_turn"}, "reply": "This mutation changes two genes. `foe_in_reach` now counts an enemy champion as a threat when it is within its own attack range plus one, instead of only within my attack range. That makes the pass-through bank and the spawn heal wait until no enemy can actually hit us. `shard_until` now gives treasure 3/5 of the shards instead of 1/2, keeping the rest of the split as before.\n\n```python\n@gene(\"s5b\", \"a visible enemy champion can hit me (its attack range + 1)\", parents=[\"s5\"])\ndef foe_in_reach() -> Bool:\n    m = here()\n    return any(dist(u.pos, m) <= u.attack_range + 1 for u in enemies())\n\n\n@gene(\"a15b\", \"shards of the first k kinds in the turn's split, treasure weighted 3/5\", parents=[\"a15\"])\ndef shard_until(k: Num) -> Num:\n    n = floor(SHOP_GOLD / 30)\n    t = floor(n * 3 / 5)\n    j = floor((n - t) / 2)\n    s = floor((n - t - j) / 2)\n    if k == 1:\n        return t\n    if k == 2:\n        return t + j\n    if k == 3:\n        return t + j + s\n    return n\n```"}, "error": "GenomeError: line 456: gene foe_in_reach redefined or shadows a builtin", "birth": 20, "accepted": false, "fingerprint": null}
